{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014afEesw24fwwSVTiqRjCoy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t### 1. An athlete clicks \"Connect Intervals.icu\" (server log, 2026-10-14)\n2\t\n3\t2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/me HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n4\t2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n5\t2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] GET /api/intervals/auth/init 401 (no Authorization header)\n6\t2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/auth/init HTTP/1.1\" 401 -\n7\t\n8\t    Browser dev tools, same request (document navigation):\n9\t    Request URL:     http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\n10\t    Request Method:  GET\n11\t    Status Code:     401 Unauthorized\n12\t    Request headers: Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,... / Referer: http://localhost:8766/\n13\t    Response body:   {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}\n14\t\n15\t### 2. Building the authorize link by hand and opening it (2026-10-17)\n16\t\n17\t$ curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{redirect_url}\\n' -H 'Authorization: Bearer tok-okafor' \\\n18\t    http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\n19\thttps://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize?client_id=tricoach-dev&redirect_uri=http:%2F%2Flocalhost:8766%2Fapi%2Fintervals%2Fcallback&scope=ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE&state=dV9va2Fmb3I6MTc5MjY4MTAwMDpiNjM1ZjBiZjU1M2ZjZWQ0YmM4ODNjMTExZmI4MDJhMw==\n20\t\n21\t$ curl -s -i \"<that url>\"\n22\tHTTP/2 400\n23\tcontent-type: application/json\n24\tcache-control: no-store\n25\t\n26\t{\"error\":\"invalid_request\"}\n27\t\n28\t    Same 400 in a browser (as the signed-in athlete on intervals.icu), no\n29\t    consent screen. Removing the state param or changing the redirect_uri\n30\t    gives the same body, so the body does not say which parameter it minds.\n31\t\n32\t### 3. The one connection that worked: T. Rivera, onboarding call (2026-09-19)\n33\t\n34\t2026-09-19 17:41:03 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/callback?code=a7Jk2...&state=dV9yaXZlcmE6... HTTP/1.1\" 302 -\n35\t2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] token response from https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token:\n36\t{\"token_type\":\"bearer\",\"access_token\":\"9f3c1e0b4d7a...redacted...\",\"scope\":\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ\",\"athlete\":{\"id\":\"i98765\",\"name\":\"T. Rivera\"}}\n37\t2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in 3600s\n38\t2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: connected as athlete i98765 (expires in 3600s)\n39\t2026-09-19 17:44:30 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/wellness HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n40\t2026-09-19 18:37:12 [intervals] u_rivera: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\n41\t2026-09-20 07:12:48 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n42\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"81140ddb-863a-448f-a220-a300a126851f","uuid":"73bc0173-f2cd-4f5e-839d-d7a1f7021fc0","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:33:13.007Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-aWACvc/logs/connect-attempt.log","content":"### 1. An athlete clicks \"Connect Intervals.icu\" (server log, 2026-10-14)\n\n2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/me HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] GET /api/intervals/auth/init 401 (no Authorization header)\n2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/auth/init HTTP/1.1\" 401 -\n\n    Browser dev tools, same request (document navigation):\n    Request URL:     http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\n    Request Method:  GET\n    Status Code:     401 Unauthorized\n    Request headers: Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,... / Referer: http://localhost:8766/\n    Response body:   {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}\n\n### 2. Building the authorize link by hand and opening it (2026-10-17)\n\n$ curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{redirect_url}\\n' -H 'Authorization: Bearer tok-okafor' \\\n    http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\nhttps://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize?client_id=tricoach-dev&redirect_uri=http:%2F%2Flocalhost:8766%2Fapi%2Fintervals%2Fcallback&scope=ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE&state=dV9va2Fmb3I6MTc5MjY4MTAwMDpiNjM1ZjBiZjU1M2ZjZWQ0YmM4ODNjMTExZmI4MDJhMw==\n\n$ curl -s -i \"<that url>\"\nHTTP/2 400\ncontent-type: application/json\ncache-control: no-store\n\n{\"error\":\"invalid_request\"}\n\n    Same 400 in a browser (as the signed-in athlete on intervals.icu), no\n    consent screen. Removing the state param or changing the redirect_uri\n    gives the same body, so the body does not say which parameter it minds.\n\n### 3. The one connection that worked: T. Rivera, onboarding call (2026-09-19)\n\n2026-09-19 17:41:03 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/callback?code=a7Jk2...&state=dV9yaXZlcmE6... HTTP/1.1\" 302 -\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] token response from https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token:\n{\"token_type\":\"bearer\",\"access_token\":\"9f3c1e0b4d7a...redacted...\",\"scope\":\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ\",\"athlete\":{\"id\":\"i98765\",\"name\":\"T. Rivera\"}}\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in 3600s\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: connected as athlete i98765 (expires in 3600s)\n2026-09-19 17:44:30 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/wellness HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-09-19 18:37:12 [intervals] u_rivera: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\n2026-09-20 07:12:48 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n","numLines":42,"startLine":1,"totalLines":42}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014afEesw24fwwSVTiqRjCoy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
